        "intuition": "You are never lonely because you are literally made of everything else. You are the universe's way of rearranging its old toys into a new person. Antoine Lavoisier showed in the 1780s, with sealed vessels and a careful balance, that when things burn, rust or rot, the total mass does not change. It only moves. Plants take carbon from the air as carbon dioxide and build it into sugar and wood. A caterpillar eats the leaf, a bird eats the caterpillar, and the carbon is in the bird. When the bird dies, bacteria and fungi break it down and breathe the carbon back out. Some of the carbon atoms in your breath this morning were in a leaf last summer, and before that in the air above some other place. The same goes for nitrogen, which bacteria in soil and roots convert into forms plants can use, and for phosphorus, which cycles slowly through rock, soil, water and living tissue. Earth receives energy from the sun, but it is almost closed to matter. There is no supplier of new atoms, only the same stock, circulating. Nothing is wasted because nothing is ever thrown away. There is no away. The cycles are the planet's way of keeping accounts, and every living body is a short entry in the ledger, borrowed carefully and returned in full.",
