        "advanced": "The Fibonacci numbers satisfy F(n) = F(n-1) + F(n-2), and Binet's formula gives F(n) as (phi to the n minus psi to the n) over the square root of 5, with psi equal to 1 minus phi. Ratios of neighbors converge to phi, about 1.618. Edouard Zeckendorf proved that every positive integer is a sum of non-consecutive Fibonacci numbers in exactly one way, and the greatest common divisor of F(m) and F(n) is F of the gcd of m and n. In botany, phyllotaxis, the study of leaf and seed arrangement, was modeled in 1979 by Helmut Vogel, who placed seed n at angle n times 137.5 degrees and radius proportional to the square root of n. The counterpoint is that Fibonacci's original rabbit model is not biology, and many claimed appearances in art or the body do not survive measurement. Where the sequence is real, it is the signature of the golden angle. This links to the nature door, where growth is arithmetic made living."
