        "intuition": "Some changes walk. Some changes run. Knowing which one you're watching changes everything. An arithmetic progression adds the same amount each step: 3, 5, 7, 9. A geometric progression multiplies by the same amount: 3, 6, 12, 24. At first they look alike. Then the second one leaves the first far behind. A famous tale says the inventor of chess asked a king for one grain of rice on the first square, two on the second, doubling on each of the 64 squares. The total is 2 to the 64th minus 1, or 18,446,744,073,709,551,615 grains. Try it with money. Receive one cent on day 1 and double it every day. On day 30 you would be handed 2 to the 29th cents, which is $5,368,709.12. Doubling ten times multiplies by 1,024, which is why 30 doublings pass a billion. Thomas Malthus argued in 1798 that populations grow geometrically while food grows only arithmetically. His forecast failed because technology changed the food side, but the arithmetic of his contrast was sound. The mind is built for the steady walk. It must be taught to see the run coming.",
