        "intuition": "Hold your hand up and look at your fingers; the ratio of each bone to the next is a tiny whisper of the same math that builds galaxies. That is poetry, and hands vary too much to prove it. The proof lives in the pentagon. Draw a regular pentagon and all five of its diagonals. The diagonal is exactly phi times the side, about 1.618, and the diagonals cut one another in that same ratio. The triangle formed by two diagonals and a side has angles 36, 72 and 72 degrees, the golden triangle, and its long sides are phi times its short one. Bisect one of the 72-degree corners and you cut off a smaller triangle of the same shape, with the same proportion, which is the self-copying of the golden ratio again. Euclid used this to construct a regular pentagon with only a compass and straightedge. In coordinates, the twelve corners of a regular icosahedron are the points with coordinates 0, plus or minus 1, plus or minus phi, in every cyclic arrangement. The number is not a mood. It is a measurement, and it sits where the five-fold symmetry sits.",
