        "intuition": "A sudden unwinding feeling in your mind, like a puzzle piece finally clicking into place after being turned the right way. Most operations have an undo. Adding 7 is undone by subtracting 7, multiplying by 3 by dividing by 3, squaring by taking the square root, and raising 10 to a power by taking a logarithm. The trick for solving any equation is to undo in reverse order, the way you take off shoes before socks because you put on socks before shoes. Take 2 times (x plus 3) equals 14. The last thing done to x was multiplying by 2, so undo that first: x plus 3 equals 7. Then undo the adding: x equals 4. Check it: 4 plus 3 is 7, and 2 times 7 is 14. Not every operation can be fully undone. Squaring loses the sign, because both 3 and negative 3 give 9, so the square root has to be told which one you want. Multiplying by zero destroys information completely, and no operation can recover what was there. A good inverse exists only where nothing has been thrown away.",
