        "intuition": "Small things matter. One kind word can change a life. Free will and determinism are woven together. Chaos theory begins with a rounding. In 1961 the meteorologist Edward Lorenz restarted a weather simulation from a printout, typing 0.506 in place of the stored 0.506127, a difference of a few parts in ten thousand. The new run drifted away from the old one until the two looked unrelated. In 1963 he published the finding, and in 1972 he gave a talk with a title asking whether a butterfly's wings in Brazil could set off a tornado in Texas. The effect is easy to see in the doubling map: take a number between 0 and 1, double it, and keep only the fractional part. Two starting values that differ by a trillionth, about 2 to the minus 40, will differ by an amount of order 1 after 40 steps, because each step doubles the gap. To see ahead twice as far, you do not need twice as good a measurement. You need a measurement a thousandfold better for each ten more steps. That is why weather forecasts lose their power after about two weeks, however good the computers. The rule is exact and the future is still unreachable. Order and unpredictability live in the same equations.",
