        "advanced": "The Bekenstein-Hawking formula is S equals k c cubed A over 4 G h-bar, where A is the horizon area, and the Bekenstein bound limits the entropy of any region by a quantity proportional to its boundary area. Juan Maldacena's 1997 conjecture of the AdS/CFT correspondence gave the principle a concrete form: a gravitational theory in a particular curved spacetime, anti-de Sitter space, is exactly equivalent to a quantum field theory without gravity on its boundary, one dimension lower. The counterpoint is that the world we live in is not anti-de Sitter space, since observations indicate a small positive cosmological constant, so whether holography holds in our universe is not established. It is a well-motivated conjecture, not a tested law, and the line about each part carrying the whole should be read as metaphor. Still, the lesson that information and geometry are tied is firmly grounded in black hole thermodynamics. This links to the mysticism door, where the picture of the whole in each part has been taught for ages."
