        "intuition": "Every action has an equal and opposite reaction. You are always connected to everything you touch. Push and be pushed. Isaac Newton stated it in the Principia in 1687: whenever body A pushes on body B with some force, B pushes back on A with exactly the same strength in the opposite direction. The two forces act on different bodies, which is why they never cancel. A skater pushes a wall and rolls backward because the wall's push acts on the skater. Take two skaters on ice, one of 60 kilograms and one of 90, who push apart. The forces are the same size, so by F equals ma the lighter skater accelerates 1.5 times as much, 90 over 60, and ends up moving 1.5 times as fast. The same holds for you and the Earth. Your weight is the Earth's pull on you, about 590 newtons if you are 60 kilograms, and you pull up on the Earth with the same force. The Earth's mass, about 6 times 10 to the 24th kilograms, means its acceleration is about 10 to the minus 22 meters per second squared, far too small to notice. The law is exact, and the mass difference hides the effect. Nothing can touch without being touched.",
