        "advanced": "The Voyager 1 probe took the Pale Blue Dot photograph on 14 February 1990, at the request of Carl Sagan, from about six billion kilometres away, and Earth shows up as less than a pixel in a band of scattered light. In 1957 Margaret and Geoffrey Burbidge, William Fowler and Fred Hoyle showed how the elements heavier than hydrogen and helium are forged in stars, and returned to space when stars die, so the carbon, oxygen and iron in a body come from earlier stars. Frank White named the overview effect in 1987 for the shift in perspective reported by astronauts who see the planet whole. Paul Piff and colleagues found in 2015 that brief experiences of awe made people feel smaller and act more generously. The limit is that a fact does not cure a feeling. The mysticism door calls the feeling of being part of everything the oceanic feeling. Even the lonely belong to the ocean."
